            <ArticleTitle>Treatment of in-stent restenosis involving a bifurcation lesion with a dedicated bifurcation device in combination with drug-eluting balloons.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>E172-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>It can be difficult to find a good treatment strategy in cases with in-stent restenosis with involvement of a bifurcation lesion. To avoid multiple stent layers and to treat the bifurcation lesion properly, the patient described in this case report was treated with a Tryton side branch stent and drug-eluting balloons. Angiographic follow-up at 8 months showed an excellent result.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
